One particularly important change

Given what you said about your website experiencing a CPU spike while the panel continued showing old/incorrect metrics, I would make Phase 3 a priority rather than treating monitoring as a cosmetic dashboard feature.

The panel should never say:

CPU: 12%

when that value is actually from 20–30 seconds ago.

Instead, every live metric should carry something like:

CPU
82%
LIVE
updated 240ms ago

or:

CPU
12%
STALE
last update 18.4s ago

That distinction is extremely important for a hosting platform.

And for resource enforcement, displayed metrics and enforced limits must come from the same authoritative node-side measurement/control layer. Otherwise you can end up with a customer apparently under their 2 GB limit while the actual workload is consuming more.
